
  <sn><md>### Hospital and City Wastes

Hospital Waste

**Hospital waste** is the waste generated from hospitals, clinics, laboratories, medical centers, and other healthcare facilities.

It can contain **infectious materials, chemicals, medicines, sharps, and general waste**.

Types of Hospital Waste

| Type                     | Examples                                               |
| ------------------------ | ------------------------------------------------------ |
| **Infectious waste**     | Blood-soaked materials, contaminated gloves, dressings |
| **Sharps**               | Needles, syringes, blades                              |
| **Pathological waste**   | Human tissues, organs                                  |
| **Pharmaceutical waste** | Expired medicines, vaccines                            |
| **Chemical waste**       | Disinfectants, laboratory chemicals                    |
| **Radioactive waste**    | Materials contaminated with radionuclides              |
| **General waste**        | Paper, food waste, packaging                           |

Effects of Hospital Waste

Improper disposal can cause:

* Spread of **infectious diseases**
* Injury from needles and other sharps
* **Soil and water pollution**
* Chemical contamination
* Toxic effects on organisms
* Antibiotic and antimicrobial resistance
* Exposure of waste workers and the public to hazardous materials

```text id="5x5f3g"
Hospital
   ↓
Hospital waste
   ↓
Improper disposal
   ↓
Soil / Water / Air
   ↓
Humans + Animals + Environment
   ↓
Health and environmental problems
```
</md></sn>
